# User Routes Refactoring Scratchpad

## 🔍 Analysis First:

### Understanding the Task Goal:
Refactor the large `users.js` file (4250 lines) into a well-organized folder structure with separate files for different route categories. The current file contains 54 different routes that handle various user-related operations, making it difficult to maintain and navigate.

### Linked/Related Files Working Together:
1. **backend/routes/users.js** - Main monolithic file with all user routes (4250 lines)
2. **backend/server.js** - Loads routes with `app.use('/api/users', require('./routes/users'))`
3. **backend/models/User.js** - User model referenced in routes
4. **backend/models/Template.js** - Template model referenced in routes
5. **backend/utils/logger.js** - Logger utility used across routes
6. **backend/middleware/validators.js** - Validation middleware (validateDeviceId, validateFirebaseUid)
7. **backend/middleware/auth.js** - Auth middleware (verifyFirebaseToken, optionalFirebaseAuth)
8. **backend/services/recommendationService.js** - Recommendation service used in routes
9. **mongoose** - Database operations throughout routes

### Key References and Import Analysis:
- **Express Router**: All routes use `router.get|post|put|delete()`
- **Shared Helper Functions**: 
  - `isValidObjectId()`
  - `handleAsyncOperation()`
  - `cleanupSubscriptionData()`
  - `safeUpdateTemplateCounts()`
  - `validateTemplateInteraction()`
- **Common Imports**: User, Template, logger, validators, auth middleware, recommendationService, mongoose
- **Route Categories Identified**:
  - **Profile Management**: profile, register, auth, complete
  - **Activity Tracking**: activity, template-view, engagement, categories
  - **Template Interactions**: likes, favorites, shares, interaction-status
  - **Subscription Management**: subscription, subscription-history, subscription-offer
  - **Session Management**: sessions, device-sessions
  - **Notifications**: notifications (mute/unmute/status), fcm-tokens, topics
  - **AI Features**: ai-usage
  - **Template Affinity**: template-affinity, ignored-templates
  - **Drafts**: drafts
  - **Analytics**: analytics/engagement
  - **Admin Operations**: block, unblock, bulk-update, delete
  - **Referrals**: referral, apply-referral
  - **Cache Management**: cached-feed
  - **Health Check**: health/template-interactions

## 📝 Scratchpad Plan:

### 🎯 Objective 
Refactor the monolithic `users.js` file into a well-organized folder structure where each category of routes is in its own file, while maintaining all functionality and preserving the same API endpoints.

### 🧩 Related Files
- **backend/routes/users.js** (main file to refactor)
- **backend/routes/users/** (new folder structure to create)
- **backend/server.js** (update route loading logic)
- All imported dependencies and middleware

### ✅ Checklist
- [x] **Analyze route categories** and group related routes together
- [x] **Create folder structure** `backend/routes/users/` with category-based files
- [x] **Extract shared utilities** into a common utilities file
- [x] **Create individual route files**:
  - [x] `profile.js` - Profile management routes
  - [x] `activity.js` - Activity tracking routes  
  - [x] `templates.js` - Template interaction routes (likes, favorites, shares)
  - [x] `subscription.js` - Subscription management routes
  - [x] `sessions.js` - Session and device management routes
  - [x] `notifications.js` - Notification and FCM token routes
  - [x] `ai.js` - AI usage routes
  - [x] `affinity.js` - Template affinity and ignored templates
  - [x] `drafts.js` - Draft management routes
  - [x] `analytics.js` - Analytics routes
  - [x] `admin.js` - Admin operations routes
  - [x] `referrals.js` - Referral system routes
  - [x] `cache.js` - Cache management routes
  - [x] `health.js` - Health check routes
  - [x] `preferences.js` - User preferences routes
- [x] **Create main index file** `backend/routes/users/index.js` to combine all routes
- [x] **Update server.js** to load the new route structure
- [x] **Test route functionality** to ensure no breaking changes
- [x] **Preserve all existing functionality** and API endpoints
- [x] **Maintain proper error handling** and middleware usage
- [x] **Ensure correct imports** in all new files
- [x] **Remove old monolithic file** once all routes are migrated

### 🧠 Context
The current `users.js` file has grown to 4250 lines with 54 different routes handling various user operations. This makes it difficult to:
- Navigate and find specific routes
- Maintain and debug code
- Review and understand functionality
- Scale and add new features

The refactoring will create a logical folder structure:
```
backend/routes/users/
├── index.js (main router that combines all sub-routes)
├── utils/
│   └── helpers.js (shared utility functions)
├── profile.js (user profile, registration, auth)
├── activity.js (activity tracking, engagement)
├── templates.js (likes, favorites, shares, interactions)
├── subscription.js (subscription management)
├── sessions.js (session and device management)
├── notifications.js (notifications, FCM tokens, topics)
├── ai.js (AI usage tracking)
├── affinity.js (template affinity, ignored templates)
├── drafts.js (draft management)
├── analytics.js (analytics and engagement stats)
├── admin.js (admin operations like block/unblock)
├── referrals.js (referral system)
├── cache.js (cached feed management)
├── health.js (health checks)
└── preferences.js (user preferences)
```

Each file will:
- Import only the dependencies it needs
- Use shared utilities from the helpers file
- Maintain the same route paths and functionality
- Use proper Express router patterns
- Include comprehensive error handling

### 🚧 Progress Log
- **Analysis Complete**: Identified 54 routes across 15 logical categories
- **Folder Structure Planned**: Created logical grouping based on functionality
- **Shared Utilities Identified**: 5 helper functions to extract
- **Route Categories Mapped**: Each route assigned to appropriate category file
- **Next**: Start implementation by creating folder structure and shared utilities

### 📋 Route Categorization Map

**Profile Management (profile.js)**:
- POST `/profile` - Update user profile
- POST `/register` - Register new user  
- POST `/auth` - Handle authentication
- GET `/:uid` - Get user data
- GET `/:uid/complete` - Get complete user profile
- PUT `/:deviceId/link-firebase` - Link Firebase UID
- POST `/:uid/bulk-update` - Bulk update user fields
- DELETE `/:uid` - Delete user account

**Activity Tracking (activity.js)**:
- PUT `/activity` - Update user activity
- PUT `/template-view` - Record template view
- POST `/engagement` - Record engagement metrics
- POST `/engagement/sync` - Sync engagement batch
- POST `/:uid/categories/visit` - Record category visit
- GET `/:uid/categories` - Get category history
- GET `/:uid/categories/stats` - Get category statistics

**Template Interactions (templates.js)**:
- GET `/:uid/templates/favorites` - Get user favorites
- GET `/:uid/templates/likes` - Get user likes  
- GET `/:uid/templates/recent` - Get recent templates
- PUT `/:uid/favorites/:templateId` - Add to favorites
- DELETE `/:uid/favorites/:templateId` - Remove from favorites
- PUT `/:uid/likes/:templateId` - Add like
- DELETE `/:uid/likes/:templateId` - Remove like
- POST `/:uid/templates/:templateId/share` - Record share
- GET `/:uid/templates/:templateId/interaction-status` - Get interaction status

**Subscription Management (subscription.js)**:
- PUT `/:uid/subscription` - Update subscription
- POST `/:uid/subscription-history` - Add subscription history
- PUT `/:uid/subscription-offer` - Update subscription offer

**Session Management (sessions.js)**:
- GET `/:uid/sessions` - Get active sessions
- POST `/:uid/sessions/invalidate` - Invalidate other sessions
- DELETE `/:uid/sessions/:deviceId` - Remove device session
- POST `/:uid/sessions/update` - Update session activity
- POST `/:uid/device-sessions` - Add device session
- DELETE `/:uid/device-sessions/:deviceId` - Remove device session
- PUT `/:uid/device-sessions/:deviceId/activity` - Update device activity

**Notifications (notifications.js)**:
- PUT `/:uid/push-preferences` - Update push preferences
- POST `/:uid/topics/subscribe` - Subscribe to topics
- POST `/:uid/topics/unsubscribe` - Unsubscribe from topics
- PUT `/:uid/notifications/mute` - Mute notifications
- PUT `/:uid/notifications/unmute` - Unmute notifications
- GET `/:uid/notifications/status` - Get notification status
- POST `/:uid/fcm-tokens` - Add FCM token
- DELETE `/:uid/fcm-tokens/:token` - Remove FCM token

**AI Features (ai.js)**:
- PUT `/:uid/ai-usage` - Update AI usage
- POST `/:uid/ai-usage/increment` - Increment AI usage

**Template Affinity (affinity.js)**:
- PUT `/:uid/template-affinity` - Update template affinity
- GET `/:uid/template-affinity/top` - Get top affinities
- POST `/:uid/ignored-templates` - Add ignored template
- DELETE `/:uid/ignored-templates/:templateId` - Remove ignored template

**Drafts (drafts.js)**:
- POST `/:uid/drafts` - Save draft
- GET `/:uid/drafts` - Get user drafts
- DELETE `/:uid/drafts/:templateId` - Delete draft

**Analytics (analytics.js)**:
- GET `/:uid/recommendations` - Get recommendations
- GET `/:uid/analytics/engagement` - Get engagement analytics

**Admin Operations (admin.js)**:
- PUT `/:uid/block` - Block user
- PUT `/:uid/unblock` - Unblock user
- POST `/:uid/bulk-update` - Bulk update user fields
- DELETE `/:uid` - Delete user account

**Referrals (referrals.js)**:
- POST `/:uid/referral` - Generate referral code
- POST `/:uid/apply-referral` - Apply referral code

**Cache Management (cache.js)**:
- PUT `/:uid/cached-feed` - Update cached feed
- GET `/:uid/cached-feed` - Get cached feed

**Health Check (health.js)**:
- GET `/health/template-interactions` - Health check

**Preferences (preferences.js)**:
- PUT `/preferences` - Update user preferences

